{"id":"edo","title":"The Edo Mystery","chapters":[{"n":1,"title":["The ",{"t":"Winner","g":"g012"}," Who Waited"],"titleJa":"第1章　待った勝者","audio":"audio/Edo01.mp3","paras":[["In 1600, a great ",{"t":"battle","g":"g014"}," ",{"t":"took place","g":"g015"}," at ",{"t":"Sekigahara","g":"g005"},". Two large ",{"t":"armies","g":"g016"}," ",{"t":"fought","g":"g018"}," to decide who would ",{"t":"rule Japan","g":"g019"},". ",{"t":"Tokugawa Ieyasu","g":"g000"}," won, but that was not ",{"t":"enough","g":"g020"},". Many ",{"t":"powerful","g":"g021"}," ",{"t":"lords","g":"g022"},", called ",{"t":"daimyo","g":"g006"},", still had their own ",{"t":"castles","g":"g024"},", ",{"t":"soldiers","g":"g026"},", and ",{"t":"land","g":"g027"},"."],["Ieyasu had waited many years for the right time to ",{"t":"act","g":"g029"},". When he was young, he was ",{"t":"sent away","g":"g030"}," from his family as a ",{"t":"hostage","g":"g010"},". He also lost ",{"t":"battles","g":"g013"}," and ",{"t":"faced","g":"g031"}," many ",{"t":"dangers","g":"g032"},". He learned an important ",{"t":"lesson","g":"g034"},": a leader must not ",{"t":"act","g":"g029"}," too quickly."],["In 1603, Ieyasu became ",{"t":"shogun","g":"g008"}," and started a new ",{"t":"government","g":"g035"}," in Edo. Today, Edo is called Tokyo. Why did he choose Edo? At that time, it was not Japan's largest city. But it was far from Kyoto and Osaka, where many of his ",{"t":"enemies","g":"g036"}," lived. Edo also had a large ",{"t":"bay","g":"g037"}," and ",{"t":"enough","g":"g020"}," ",{"t":"land","g":"g027"}," for a new city."],["This was the first ",{"t":"secret","g":"g038"},": Ieyasu chose a place where he could build a new ",{"t":"center of power","g":"g039"},"."]],"ja":["1600年、関ヶ原で大きな戦いが起こりました。だれが日本を治めるかを決めるために、2つの大きな軍が戦いました。徳川家康が勝ちましたが、それだけでは十分ではありませんでした。大名とよばれる力の強い領主たちは、まだ自分の城と兵士と領地をもっていたのです。","家康は、動くのにちょうどよい時を、何年も待ってきました。若いころ、家康は人質として家族のもとから遠くへやられました。戦いに負けたこともあり、たくさんの危険にも出あいました。家康は大切な教訓を学びました。それは「上に立つ者は、急いで動いてはいけない」ということです。","1603年、家康は将軍になり、江戸で新しい政府を始めました。江戸は今の東京です。なぜ家康は江戸を選んだのでしょう。そのころ、江戸は日本でいちばん大きな町ではありませんでした。でも、家康の敵がたくさんいた京都や大阪からは遠くはなれていました。また、江戸には大きな湾があり、新しい町をつくるのに十分な土地もありました。","これが1つ目の秘密です。家康は、新しい権力の中心をつくれる場所を選んだのです。"]},{"n":2,"title":["Friends, ",{"t":"Enemies","g":"g036"},", and ",{"t":"Land","g":"g027"}],"titleJa":"第2章　味方と敵と領地","audio":"audio/Edo02.mp3","paras":[["After ",{"t":"Sekigahara","g":"g005"},", Ieyasu moved many ",{"t":"daimyo","g":"g006"}," to new ",{"t":"lands","g":"g028"},". He gave important ",{"t":"areas","g":"g041"}," to his family and his oldest ",{"t":"supporters","g":"g042"},". These ",{"t":"trusted","g":"g043"}," ",{"t":"lords","g":"g022"}," lived near Edo or ",{"t":"along","g":"g044"}," important roads."],[{"t":"Lords","g":"g022"}," who joined Ieyasu only after the ",{"t":"battle","g":"g014"}," began were ",{"t":"treated","g":"g045"}," ",{"t":"differently","g":"g046"},". Their ",{"t":"lands","g":"g028"}," were often far from Edo. Ieyasu did not always ",{"t":"destroy","g":"g047"}," his ",{"t":"enemies","g":"g036"},". He carefully decided where they lived."],["He also kept rich ",{"t":"lands","g":"g028"}," for the Tokugawa family. These ",{"t":"lands","g":"g028"}," gave his ",{"t":"government","g":"g035"}," money and rice."],["It was like a big game of ",{"t":"chess","g":"g049"},". Every ",{"t":"lord","g":"g023"}," had a place, and every place had a ",{"t":"purpose","g":"g050"},"."],["This was the second ",{"t":"secret","g":"g038"},": Ieyasu used ",{"t":"land","g":"g027"}," to ",{"t":"control","g":"g051"}," both his friends and his ",{"t":"possible","g":"g053"}," ",{"t":"enemies","g":"g036"},"."]],"ja":["関ヶ原のあと、家康はたくさんの大名を新しい領地に移しました。大切な地域は、自分の一族や昔からの味方にあたえました。こうした信頼できる大名たちは、江戸の近くや大事な道に沿った所に住みました。","戦いが始まってから家康の味方についた大名は、ちがうあつかいを受けました。その領地は、江戸から遠いことが多かったのです。家康はいつも敵をほろぼしたわけではありません。どこに住まわせるかを、注意深く決めたのです。","家康はまた、豊かな土地を徳川家のものとして手もとに残しました。これらの土地から、政府はお金と米を得ました。","それは大きなチェスのゲームのようでした。どの大名にも置き場所があり、どの場所にも目的があったのです。","これが2つ目の秘密です。家康は土地を使って、味方も、敵になるかもしれない相手も、おさえたのです。"]},{"n":3,"title":["The ",{"t":"Shadow","g":"g054"}," of Osaka ",{"t":"Castle","g":"g025"}],"titleJa":"第3章　大坂城のかげ","audio":"audio/Edo03.mp3","paras":[["Ieyasu was ",{"t":"shogun","g":"g008"},", but one great ",{"t":"danger","g":"g033"}," ",{"t":"remained","g":"g055"},". ",{"t":"Toyotomi Hideyori","g":"g002"},", the son of ",{"t":"Toyotomi Hideyoshi","g":"g001"},", lived in Osaka ",{"t":"Castle","g":"g025"},". Many people still thought the Toyotomi family should ",{"t":"rule Japan","g":"g019"},"."],["Osaka ",{"t":"Castle","g":"g025"}," was strong, and many ",{"t":"warriors","g":"g056"}," ",{"t":"against","g":"g057"}," the Tokugawa family ",{"t":"gathered","g":"g058"}," there. Ieyasu knew that Japan could not have two ",{"t":"centers of power","g":"g040"},"."],["In 1614 and 1615, the Tokugawa ",{"t":"army","g":"g017"}," ",{"t":"attacked","g":"g059"}," Osaka ",{"t":"Castle","g":"g025"},". The ",{"t":"castle","g":"g025"}," ",{"t":"fell","g":"g060"},", and the Toyotomi family was ",{"t":"destroyed","g":"g048"},"."],["It was a ",{"t":"cruel","g":"g061"}," ending, but now no family was strong ",{"t":"enough","g":"g020"}," to fight the Tokugawa."],["Ieyasu died in 1616, only one year later. But he had already made his son ",{"t":"Hidetada","g":"g003"}," the new ",{"t":"shogun","g":"g008"},", so people knew ",{"t":"Tokugawa rule","g":"g062"}," would ",{"t":"continue","g":"g063"},"."],["This was the third ",{"t":"secret","g":"g038"},": he ",{"t":"removed","g":"g064"}," his ",{"t":"greatest rival","g":"g065"}," and ",{"t":"prepared","g":"g066"}," a ",{"t":"peaceful","g":"g067"}," change of leaders."]],"ja":["家康は将軍になりましたが、大きな危険が1つ残っていました。豊臣秀吉の息子、豊臣秀頼が大坂城に住んでいたのです。多くの人は、まだ豊臣家が日本を治めるべきだと考えていました。","大坂城は守りが固く、徳川家に反対する武士がたくさん集まっていました。家康は、日本に権力の中心が2つあってはならないとわかっていました。","1614年と1615年、徳川の軍は大坂城を攻めました。城は落ち、豊臣家はほろびました。","それはむごい終わり方でした。しかしこれで、徳川と戦えるほど強い一族はいなくなりました。","家康は、そのわずか1年後の1616年に亡くなりました。でも、家康はすでに息子の秀忠を新しい将軍にしていたので、人々は徳川の支配が続くとわかっていました。","これが3つ目の秘密です。家康はいちばんの敵を取りのぞき、争いなく次の指導者に引きつぐ準備をしたのです。"]},{"n":4,"title":["A ",{"t":"Web","g":"g068"}," Around the ",{"t":"Daimyo","g":"g006"}],"titleJa":"第4章　大名をとりかこむ網","audio":"audio/Edo04.mp3","paras":[["Ieyasu did not finish the Tokugawa ",{"t":"system","g":"g070"}," ",{"t":"alone","g":"g069"},". His son ",{"t":"Hidetada","g":"g003"}," and his ",{"t":"grandson","g":"g071"}," ",{"t":"Iemitsu","g":"g004"}," made it stronger."],["The ",{"t":"government","g":"g035"}," made rules for the ",{"t":"daimyo","g":"g006"},". They needed ",{"t":"permission","g":"g072"}," to ",{"t":"repair","g":"g073"}," ",{"t":"castles","g":"g024"}," or for important ",{"t":"marriages","g":"g074"},". Each ",{"t":"daimyo","g":"g006"}," could have only one ",{"t":"castle","g":"g025"}," in his ",{"t":"land","g":"g027"},"."],["Later, under ",{"t":"Iemitsu","g":"g004"},", a ",{"t":"system","g":"g070"}," called ",{"t":"sankin-kotai","g":"g009"}," became a ",{"t":"regular duty","g":"g075"},". ",{"t":"Daimyo","g":"g006"}," had to live in Edo ",{"t":"every other year","g":"g076"},". Their ",{"t":"wives","g":"g077"}," and children usually stayed in Edo."],["Traveling with many ",{"t":"servants","g":"g078"}," ",{"t":"cost","g":"g079"}," a lot of money, so the ",{"t":"daimyo","g":"g006"}," had ",{"t":"less","g":"g080"}," money for large ",{"t":"armies","g":"g016"},". The ",{"t":"shogun","g":"g008"}," could also watch them ",{"t":"closely","g":"g081"},"."],["There was another ",{"t":"effect","g":"g082"},", too. Roads, towns, shops, and ",{"t":"inns","g":"g011"}," grew because so many people traveled ",{"t":"across","g":"g083"}," Japan."],["This was the fourth ",{"t":"secret","g":"g038"},": the Tokugawa family ",{"t":"controlled","g":"g052"}," the ",{"t":"daimyo","g":"g006"}," and also helped ",{"t":"trade","g":"g084"}," and travel grow."]],"ja":["徳川のしくみは、家康ひとりで完成したわけではありません。息子の秀忠と孫の家光が、それをもっと強いものにしました。","政府は大名のための決まりをつくりました。大名は、城を修理するときや、大切な結婚をするときに、許可が必要でした。また、大名は自分の領地に城を1つしかもてませんでした。","その後、家光のときに、参勤交代というしくみが決まった務めになりました。大名は1年おきに江戸に住まなければなりませんでした。大名の妻や子どもは、ふつう江戸にとどまりました。","たくさんの家来を連れて旅をするには、多くのお金がかかりました。そのため、大名は大きな軍をもつためのお金が少なくなりました。将軍は大名をしっかり見はることもできました。","このしくみには、別の効果もありました。とても多くの人が日本じゅうを旅したので、道や町、店、宿屋が発展したのです。","これが4つ目の秘密です。徳川家は大名をおさえながら、商売や旅がさかんになるのも助けたのです。"]},{"n":5,"title":["The ",{"t":"Final","g":"g086"}," Answer"],"titleJa":"第5章　最後の答え","audio":"audio/Edo05.mp3","paras":[["For more than 260 years, Japan had no large war between ",{"t":"powerful","g":"g021"}," ",{"t":"daimyo","g":"g006"},". Farmers grew more rice, cities grew, and ",{"t":"merchants","g":"g087"}," became richer. Edo became one of the largest cities in the world."],["The ",{"t":"government","g":"g035"}," ",{"t":"controlled","g":"g052"}," ",{"t":"contact","g":"g088"}," with other countries, but Japan was not ",{"t":"completely closed","g":"g089"},". It ",{"t":"still","g":"g100"}," ",{"t":"traded","g":"g085"}," with China, Korea, the Netherlands, and others through a few ",{"t":"ports","g":"g090"},". The Tokugawa leaders wanted ",{"t":"trade","g":"g084"},", but not ",{"t":"danger","g":"g033"}," from other countries."],["So, what was the ",{"t":"secret","g":"g038"}," of Edo?"],["There was not just one answer. Ieyasu was ",{"t":"patient","g":"g091"},". He chose Edo carefully, ",{"t":"controlled","g":"g052"}," important ",{"t":"lands","g":"g028"},", ",{"t":"defeated","g":"g092"}," the Toyotomi family, and ",{"t":"prepared","g":"g066"}," his son to rule. Later ",{"t":"shoguns","g":"g007"}," added new rules. Peace, a ",{"t":"growing economy","g":"g093"},", good roads, and strong ",{"t":"control","g":"g051"}," all ",{"t":"supported","g":"g094"}," the ",{"t":"government","g":"g035"},"."],["The Tokugawa ",{"t":"government","g":"g035"}," was not ",{"t":"perfect","g":"g095"},". People were ",{"t":"divided into","g":"g096"}," ",{"t":"strict classes","g":"g097"},", and many paid heavy ",{"t":"taxes","g":"g098"}," and had little ",{"t":"freedom","g":"g099"},". ",{"t":"Still","g":"g100"},", its leaders understood something important: winning power and keeping power are different problems."],["Ieyasu won Japan through war, but the Tokugawa family kept it through ",{"t":"planning","g":"g101"},", rules, and ",{"t":"patience","g":"g102"},". That was the real ",{"t":"secret","g":"g038"}," of Edo."]],"ja":["260年以上のあいだ、日本では力の強い大名どうしの大きな戦争がありませんでした。農民はより多くの米を作り、町は大きくなり、商人は豊かになりました。江戸は世界でも有数の大きな都市になりました。","政府はほかの国とのつきあいをきびしく管理しましたが、日本は完全に閉ざされていたわけではありません。いくつかの港を通して、中国、朝鮮、オランダなどとの貿易は続いていました。徳川の指導者たちは、貿易はしたいけれど、ほかの国から危険がおよぶのはさけたいと考えていたのです。","では、江戸の秘密とは何だったのでしょう。","答えは1つだけではありません。家康はがまん強い人でした。江戸を注意深く選び、大切な土地をおさえ、豊臣家を打ち負かし、息子が国を治められるように準備しました。その後の将軍たちは、新しい決まりを加えました。平和、成長する経済、よい道、そして強い支配が、すべてこの政府をささえたのです。","徳川の政府は完全なものではありませんでした。人々はきびしい身分に分けられ、多くの人が重い税をはらい、自由もほとんどありませんでした。それでも、その指導者たちは大切なことをわかっていました。それは、力を手に入れることと、力を守り続けることは、別の問題だということです。","家康は戦争によって日本を手に入れましたが、徳川家は計画と決まりと忍耐によって、それを守り続けました。それこそが、江戸の本当の秘密だったのです。"]}],"subtitle":"How Did Ieyasu Build a Government That Lasted for More Than 260 Years?","gloss":{"g000":{"w":"Tokugawa Ieyasu","ja":"徳川家康（江戸幕府を開いた人。1543〜1616年）"},"g001":{"w":"Toyotomi Hideyoshi","ja":"豊臣秀吉（家康の前に日本を治めた人）"},"g002":{"w":"Toyotomi Hideyori","ja":"豊臣秀頼（秀吉の息子）"},"g003":{"w":"Hidetada","ja":"徳川秀忠（家康の息子。2代目の将軍）"},"g004":{"w":"Iemitsu","ja":"徳川家光（家康の孫。3代目の将軍）"},"g005":{"w":"Sekigahara","ja":"関ヶ原（今の岐阜県。1600年に大きな戦いがあった所）"},"g006":{"w":"daimyo","ja":"大名（自分の領地と家来をもつ武士）"},"g007":{"w":"shoguns","base":"shogun","ja":"将軍たち"},"g008":{"w":"shogun","ja":"将軍（武士の政府のいちばん上の人）"},"g009":{"w":"sankin-kotai","ja":"参勤交代（大名が江戸と自分の領地を行き来する決まり）"},"g010":{"w":"hostage","ja":"人質"},"g011":{"w":"inns","base":"inn","ja":"宿屋"},"g012":{"w":"Winner","base":"winner","ja":"勝った人、勝者"},"g013":{"w":"battles","base":"battle","ja":"戦い"},"g014":{"w":"battle","ja":"戦い"},"g015":{"w":"took place","base":"take place","ja":"起こった、行われた"},"g016":{"w":"armies","base":"army","ja":"軍隊"},"g017":{"w":"army","ja":"軍隊"},"g018":{"w":"fought","base":"fight","ja":"戦った"},"g019":{"w":"rule Japan","ja":"日本を治める（rule＝治める、支配する）"},"g020":{"w":"enough","ja":"十分な、十分に（strong enough to 〜＝〜できるほど強い）"},"g021":{"w":"powerful","ja":"力の強い"},"g022":{"w":"lords","base":"lord","ja":"大名、領主（土地を治める人）"},"g023":{"w":"lord","ja":"大名、領主（土地を治める人）"},"g024":{"w":"castles","base":"castle","ja":"城"},"g025":{"w":"castle","ja":"城"},"g026":{"w":"soldiers","base":"soldier","ja":"兵士"},"g027":{"w":"land","ja":"土地、領地"},"g028":{"w":"lands","base":"land","ja":"領地（大名が治める土地）"},"g029":{"w":"act","ja":"行動する"},"g030":{"w":"sent away","base":"send away","ja":"（家族のもとから）遠くへやられた"},"g031":{"w":"faced","base":"face","ja":"（危険などに）直面した、出あった"},"g032":{"w":"dangers","base":"danger","ja":"危険"},"g033":{"w":"danger","ja":"危険"},"g034":{"w":"lesson","ja":"教訓（経験から学んだ大切なこと）"},"g035":{"w":"government","ja":"政府（ここでは幕府）"},"g036":{"w":"enemies","base":"enemy","ja":"敵"},"g037":{"w":"bay","ja":"湾（海が陸に入りこんだ所）"},"g038":{"w":"secret","ja":"秘密、ひけつ"},"g039":{"w":"center of power","ja":"権力の中心（power＝力、権力）"},"g040":{"w":"centers of power","base":"center of power","ja":"権力の中心（power＝力、権力）"},"g041":{"w":"areas","base":"area","ja":"地域"},"g042":{"w":"supporters","base":"supporter","ja":"味方、支持者"},"g043":{"w":"trusted","base":"trust","ja":"信頼された"},"g044":{"w":"along","ja":"〜に沿って"},"g045":{"w":"treated","base":"treat","ja":"あつかわれた"},"g046":{"w":"differently","ja":"ちがうように"},"g047":{"w":"destroy","ja":"ほろぼす、こわす"},"g048":{"w":"destroyed","base":"destroy","ja":"ほろぼされた"},"g049":{"w":"chess","ja":"チェス（西洋の将棋）"},"g050":{"w":"purpose","ja":"目的、役目"},"g051":{"w":"control","ja":"支配する、管理する（名詞では「支配」）"},"g052":{"w":"controlled","base":"control","ja":"支配した、管理した"},"g053":{"w":"possible","ja":"〜になるかもしれない"},"g054":{"w":"Shadow","base":"shadow","ja":"かげ（ここでは「不安のもと」の意味）"},"g055":{"w":"remained","base":"remain","ja":"残っていた"},"g056":{"w":"warriors","base":"warrior","ja":"武士、戦士"},"g057":{"w":"against","ja":"〜に反対して、〜に敵対して"},"g058":{"w":"gathered","base":"gather","ja":"集まった"},"g059":{"w":"attacked","base":"attack","ja":"攻撃した"},"g060":{"w":"fell","base":"fall","ja":"（城が）落ちた、攻め落とされた"},"g061":{"w":"cruel","ja":"むごい、ひどい"},"g062":{"w":"Tokugawa rule","ja":"徳川の支配（rule＝支配）"},"g063":{"w":"continue","ja":"続く"},"g064":{"w":"removed","base":"remove","ja":"取りのぞいた"},"g065":{"w":"greatest rival","ja":"いちばんのライバル、最大の敵（rival＝競争相手）"},"g066":{"w":"prepared","base":"prepare","ja":"準備した"},"g067":{"w":"peaceful","ja":"平和な、争いのない"},"g068":{"w":"Web","base":"web","ja":"クモの巣、網（ここでは大名をしばる決まりのたとえ）"},"g069":{"w":"alone","ja":"ひとりで"},"g070":{"w":"system","ja":"しくみ、制度"},"g071":{"w":"grandson","ja":"孫（男）"},"g072":{"w":"permission","ja":"許可"},"g073":{"w":"repair","ja":"修理する"},"g074":{"w":"marriages","base":"marriage","ja":"結婚"},"g075":{"w":"regular duty","ja":"決まった務め（regular＝決まった、duty＝務め）"},"g076":{"w":"every other year","ja":"1年おきに"},"g077":{"w":"wives","base":"wife","ja":"妻たち（wife の複数形）"},"g078":{"w":"servants","base":"servant","ja":"家来、使用人"},"g079":{"w":"cost","ja":"（お金が）かかった"},"g080":{"w":"less","ja":"より少ない"},"g081":{"w":"closely","ja":"注意深く、しっかりと"},"g082":{"w":"effect","ja":"結果、効果"},"g083":{"w":"across","ja":"〜じゅうを、〜を横切って"},"g084":{"w":"trade","ja":"商売、貿易"},"g085":{"w":"traded","base":"trade","ja":"貿易をした"},"g086":{"w":"Final","base":"final","ja":"最後の"},"g087":{"w":"merchants","base":"merchant","ja":"商人"},"g088":{"w":"contact","ja":"つきあい、交流"},"g089":{"w":"completely closed","ja":"完全に閉ざされた（completely＝完全に）"},"g090":{"w":"ports","base":"port","ja":"港"},"g091":{"w":"patient","ja":"がまん強い"},"g092":{"w":"defeated","base":"defeat","ja":"打ち負かした"},"g093":{"w":"growing economy","ja":"成長する経済（economy＝経済）"},"g094":{"w":"supported","base":"support","ja":"ささえた"},"g095":{"w":"perfect","ja":"完全な、欠点のない"},"g096":{"w":"divided into","base":"divide into","ja":"〜に分けられた"},"g097":{"w":"strict classes","ja":"きびしい身分（class＝身分。武士・農民・町人など）"},"g098":{"w":"taxes","base":"tax","ja":"税金（ここでは年貢など）"},"g099":{"w":"freedom","ja":"自由"},"g100":{"w":"Still","base":"still","ja":"それでも"},"g101":{"w":"planning","base":"plan","ja":"計画すること"},"g102":{"w":"patience","ja":"がまん強さ、忍耐"}}}